                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a7fe825-567a-35ca-9911-b1f357b029fd",
                        "entry_id": "f7e6ca7a-cdc8-30b1-bda6-c18d6dafd7c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui apporte le salut, qui est capable de sauver."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f54daa15-8af2-4e4a-ac50-ed207e493ec6",
                                "sense_id": "4a7fe825-567a-35ca-9911-b1f357b029fd",
                                "text": "Au Moyen Âge, à cet endroit où le gave se rétrécit, une jeune fille aurait été sauvée de la noyade par un « beau rameau » - « betharram » en béarnais - tendu par Marie et Jésus. Ce rameau salvifique est représenté au pied de la Vierge à l’Enfant […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b33486c-933c-412e-9bd1-7cd8487bcaea",
                                "sense_id": "4a7fe825-567a-35ca-9911-b1f357b029fd",
                                "text": "Pour le Japon du VIIᵉ siècle, la vie est plutôt une gigantesque école où l’on apprend chaque jour une vingtaine d’idéogrammes chinois, le nom d’une nouvelle étoile, une recette fumigatoire ou un moyen salvifique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ebd5e3d-1f99-374d-8cd0-66ae424536f6",
                        "entry_id": "f7e6ca7a-cdc8-30b1-bda6-c18d6dafd7c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est capable de sauver l’âme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d2463b4-2546-4fc6-8428-d23564d0b907",
                                "sense_id": "2ebd5e3d-1f99-374d-8cd0-66ae424536f6",
                                "text": "Jésus Christ médiateur et sauveur de la Création, confirme que la Création est l’œuvre très bonne de Dieu. Sont ainsi tenues ensemble les actions créatrices et salvifiques. La Création ne peut-être séparée du Salut."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "11dd04cd-4ff4-4b93-832e-f0dc1edb3e8e",
                        "source_entry_id": "f7e6ca7a-cdc8-30b1-bda6-c18d6dafd7c8",
                        "target_lang_word": "salvific",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "salvific",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "867bf84f-f63a-3aff-8aad-66c8dc4f2062",
                                        "entry_id": "7b49d379-92ee-3c2d-94f9-73b1a4bff76e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able or intending to provide salvation or redemption."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b4d8b8d-4d8e-4381-8255-e4262161f4f1",
                                                "sense_id": "867bf84f-f63a-3aff-8aad-66c8dc4f2062",
                                                "text": "Less well recognized, however, is the central role played in much of early medieval Pure Land Buddhism by deathbed practices and accompanying beliefs about the radical salvific power of one's last nenbutsu, whether understood as the contemplation of the Buddha Amitābha (or Amitāyus, Jpn. Amida) or the invocation of his name."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe71a0b6-810f-4eb6-8623-3d5338306e2f",
                                                "sense_id": "867bf84f-f63a-3aff-8aad-66c8dc4f2062",
                                                "text": "2012, Magdalen Ross (translator), Athanasius Schneider, 7: Adoration and the Sacred Liturgy, Alcuin Reid (editor), From Eucharistic Adoration to Evangelization, Continuum Books (Burns & Oates), page 84,\nThe fragrance [of this sacrifice] is the most pleasing perfume, the most holy, the most salvific and the most beautiful; […] ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55376b4b-8e60-4def-873c-69679da6d1db",
                                                "sense_id": "867bf84f-f63a-3aff-8aad-66c8dc4f2062",
                                                "text": "2017, Boris Jakim (translator), Pavel Florensky, Early Religious Writings, 1903-1909, William B. Eerdmans Publishing Company, page 149,\n[…] participation in the liturgy is more salvific than the reading of the Bible; the performance of cult is more important than charitable giving."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ccbbc4f-b9ba-4eac-b43c-93c32e4ada4d",
                                                "sense_id": "867bf84f-f63a-3aff-8aad-66c8dc4f2062",
                                                "text": "2019, Ernest L. Gibson, Salvific Manhood, University of Nebraska Press, page 93,\nNevertheless, as this love truly begins to show itself, as the men became more salvific for each other, David pulls back."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
